    "font" : "SFRM1000",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. Each term bj in the polynomial modulo p counts exactly those independent sets with nontrivial stabilizers. By definition, these are precisely sets that are fixed by some non-identity element h ∈ Hp. Thus, summing over non-identity elements gives the generating function for fixed independent sets, proving the equivalence stated in (ii)(c) of Theorem 3.1."
