    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 305.529, 547.136, 338.348 ],
    "font" : "SFBX1000",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Polynomial Congruences and Frobenius Completion Let us examine when the congruence I(Cn⊠d,x) ≡ (x + 1)m (mod p) holds for some m ≤ pd:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 17,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 268.02, 540.001, 306.468 ],
    "font" : "SFTI1000",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proposition 3.5. Let n be composite with prime divisor p. Then I(Cn⊠d,x) ≡ c · (x + 1)m (mod p) for some constant c ∈ F×p and m ≤ pd if and only if the only Hp-invariant independent sets are those consisting entirely of vertices fixed point wise by the action of Hp."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 18,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 236.179, 540.0, 260.667 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1000",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proof. Let Fp be the set of all independent sets that are fixed by at least one non-identity element of Hp. The generating function for these sets is:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 21,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 326.256, 212.948, 341.955, 225.034 ],
