    "font size" : 6.974,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "x|S|"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 19,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 269.547, 212.975, 301.298, 222.938 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "F(x) ="
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 304.063, 196.929, 324.097, 209.015 ],
    "font" : "CMSY7",
    "font size" : 6.974,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "S∈Fp"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 22,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 147.701, 540.001, 196.099 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1000",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "By the orbit-stabilizer theorem, each Hp-invariant independent set belongs to an orbit whose size divides p, leading to constraints on I(Cn⊠d,x). When Fp contains only independent sets consisting of vertices fixed point wise by Hp, F(x) takes the form (x+1)m −1 for some m ≤ pd, representing all possible subsets of the fixed vertex set minus the empty set."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 23,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 86.944, 135.746, 230.121, 148.279 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1000",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Under these conditions, we have:"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 24,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 210.999, 105.469, 401.001, 126.832 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "I(Cn⊠d,x) ≡ 1 + F(x) ≡ (x + 1)m (mod p)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 81.947, 540.0, 108.401 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1000",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Conversely, if I(Cn⊠d,x) ≡ c · (x + 1)m (mod p), then Fp must correspond to the structure (x + 1)m − 1, implying that the only invariant sets are those built from fixed vertices."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 26,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 86.944, 69.992, 302.523, 82.525 ],
